{
	quest.011FAAAEDB15C1D2.quest_desc: [
		"Ever thought it was annoying that glass blocks don't have a effective tool or that they need Silk Touch to be obtained? The &6Scribe&r fixes that!"
		""
		"It's able to mine any crystalline blocks quickly, even Silk Touching them! What are those crystalline blocks, you ask? It's glass, panes, ice, amethyst, quartz and even obsidian!"
	]
	quest.0330070323804BC3.quest_desc: [
		"Want what the trash cans do, but in one block? There's the &6Ultimate Trash Can&r. It can void items, fluid and power!"
		""
		"No, but seriously. Why would you ever want to void power?"
	]
	quest.0403366A7C868CD4.quest_desc: ["The &6Wand Capacity Template&r allows you to upgrade a &eMech Trowel&r's &9Wand&r mode to support up to 128 blocks."]
	quest.088CD77FCC986860.quest_desc: ["&6Template Managers&r allows you to save any structure you copy with the &eCopy Paste Gadget&r to then reuse them later or share with others. Place the gadget inside with some paper and you'll be able to save the structure to a Blueprint."]
	quest.0924EE320FE71B8E.quest_desc: ["This works similarly to the &eCopy Paste Gadget&r, except it removes from an area to places it into another. Make sure the area you're pasting into is cleared otherwise those blocks will be voided when the structure is pasted in!"]
	quest.0A24EB9FAE677980.quest_desc: ["&6Basic Item Collectors&r instantly pick up any item in their configurable range and place them in the inventory of the block they're attached to. They don't have an inventory of their own, so they HAVE to be attached to a container."]
	quest.0AF1FD2345C2C694.quest_desc: [
		"Got a structure you want to build over and over again? Then this gadget is the tool for the job!"
		"First select a structure you want to copy by right clicking a corner and then sneak right clicking the other corner in &bCopy mode&r. Now change the gadget's mode to &bPaste mode&r and you can now paste in the structure you just copied, provided you have the blocks in your inventory."
	]
	quest.0BB06B2A2A28DC42.quest_desc: ["&6Bird Catcherss&r work like the &eAnimal Cages&r, except for flying animals, such as bees."]
	quest.0F1AFA3F130C3206.quest_desc: [
		"&6Animal Cages&r are able to capture any type of animal by simply right clicking on the animal. They have a near infinite capacity! If you want to release one animal, simply sneak right click on a block."
		""
		"They're main use is to be placed inside of &eAnimal Pens&r."
	]
	quest.101C742E94859998.quest_desc: ["&eFeral Flare Lanterns&r normally remove the light sources they spawn when they're broken, but that's sometimes not the case. &6Frozen Pearls&r fixes that."]
	quest.181283E8D770BFD4.quest_desc: ["Allows you to quickly place down a series of blocks, either on the surface you're aiming at or placing blocks from where you're aiming at towards you."]
	quest.1B566C48BD66EE71.quest_desc: ["Makes replacing blocks with others a breeze. Good for texturing walls or just to replace the blocks in a walls of a hole you dug in general."]
	quest.1C493B201A7C827A.quest_desc: ["&6Nature's Compass&r allows you to search for a specific biome. Select your favorite biome and the compass will point you towards it and how far away it is. That is if it has found the biome."]
	quest.1CB0EF8F70C3AAA5.quest_desc: [
		"&6PokéNavs&r will tell you what Pokémon are currently able to spawn at your current location. It even allows you track a Pokémon you select, guiding you to it's position."
		""
		"&6Old PokéNav&r is a broken down PokéNav that you can find through looting chests and can be repaired to get a PokéNav cheaper!"
	]
	quest.1CB0EF8F70C3AAA5.title: "PokéNav"
	quest.221362723A264685.quest_desc: [
		"&6Energy Trash Cans&r simply just use energy and do nothing with it."
		""
		"Not sure why you would ever want this, but it's here."
	]
	quest.329FE5C4FF7344C6.quest_desc: ["Want a bit of extra range when working with the &eMech Trowel&r? Combine it with an &6Extended Range Template&r to get 4 extra blocks of reach!"]
	quest.32D5E58655B30ED6.quest_desc: ["The &6Bartering Station&r will take any gold inside of it and give them to Piglins nearby. Any items that Piglins trade are then magically teleported into the station."]
	quest.39455C6BBA6D751F.quest_desc: ["&6Advanced Item Collectors&r have a bigger range that they can be configured to. They also allow filtering so that they only pick up certain items."]
	quest.3AA452ACB3A095EF.quest_desc: [
		"Ever wondered how much damage you do and didn't want to kill accidentally your friends? &0(Or maybe you just don't have any friends?)&r"
		"The &6Target Dummy&r comes to the rescue! Place it down and give it a few whacks, the dummy will display how much damage a hit did and how much DPS you're doing. "
		""
		"Sneak left click the dummy to remove it."
		""
		"Equip it with armor to give it armor values."
		"Equip it with an undead mob head to make it undead."
		"Equip it with a banner to make it enter Boss Mode, a mode where you have to 'kill' the dummy as quickly as possible."
	]
	quest.3C8008863F4155D9.quest_desc: [
		"&6Building Gadgets&r is a mod that adds various tools that help around building."
		""
		"Check out your key binds and look for a \"Settings Menu\" key. This is the most important key you will need to know when using the building gadgets as it allows you to configure your gadgets."
		""
		"All of these devices require power."
		""
		"The provided guide book, \"Gadgets for Derps\", will go into more detail about these gadgets."
	]
	quest.3C8008863F4155D9.title: "Building Gadgets"
	quest.458B622F12812BF2.quest_desc: [
		"If you have multiple colors of a &echalk&r, you can store them inside of a &6Chalk Box&r to save on inventory space. "
		""
		"Right clicking in the air will open a menu where you can insert the chalk. You can also insert chalk into the box similar to how you insert items into bundles."
		""
		"Right clicking a block will then draw with whatever chalk you have currently selected. Sneaking at the same time will bring the same menu where you can select a drawing."
		""
		"Sneak right clicking in the air will cycle between the chalk inside of the box."
		""
		"The box also allows you to use &bGlow Ink Sacs&r or &bGlowstone Dust&r more efficiently. Inserting one of them will fill up a bar that gradually gets used up whenever you draw. "
	]
	quest.4A1B621AA82791C6.quest_desc: ["Get iron tools to unlock this drawing."]
	quest.4A1B621AA82791C6.title: "Pickaxe"
	quest.5144BDADF125B298.quest_desc: ["Finding a skull will unlock this drawing."]
	quest.5144BDADF125B298.title: "Skull"
	quest.528D1A2D00FBCF72.quest_desc: ["&6Aquariums&r work like the regular &eAnimal Pens&r, just for water animals."]
	quest.548C0252A4207246.quest_desc: [
		"&6Animal Pens&r basically condense giant in-world pens to just a single block, reducing lag."
		""
		"The pens retain most animals' functionalities, such as shearing sheep, collecting eggs (which needs a bucket) and even breeding. If you sneak while looking at a pen, you will see their cooldowns and what item to use on the animal."
		""
		"You can kill one animal at a time by left clicking a weapon on the pen."
	]
	quest.548C0252A4207246.title: "Animal Pens"
	quest.573E922C84844A52.quest_desc: [
		"&6Item Trash Cans&r void any items inserted inside of them. Great for factories that produce unwanted byproducts, like Flint."
		""
		"They can also be filtered so you're sure nothing of value gets accidentally voided."
	]
	quest.57B55E48CEB175B0.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Mech Trowel&r allows you to place blocks randomly. It got three modes: &9Quick&r, &9Pallete&r and &9Wand&r."
		""
		"Quick will simply uses the blocks from your hotbar."
		""
		"Palette will use the blocks configured inside of its menu. These blocks can even be configured, allowing you to give each block a percentage on how likely they should be placed. You can even save up to 25 palette, each with 28 blocks!"
		""
		"The Mech Trowel has more up its sleeve:"
		"- Replace Mode that replaces blocks instead"
		"- Gradients that allow you to smoothly transition from one palette to another between points"
		"- Can even place Copycats (even those from Copycats+) and Framed Blocks with blocks already filled in (Left click on the Copycat/Framed Block inside of the palette GUI to configure)"
		"- Extracts blocks inside of Shulker Boxes and Backpacks"
	]
	quest.57FFF05E58358F88.quest_desc: ["&6Mega Torches&r prevent any monster in a big radius around itself from spawning. Just place one in a dark area and you won't have to worry about lighting it up."]
	quest.5909105DACB265C7.quest_desc: ["&6PokéFinder&r places a minimap at the bottom right corner of your screen, displaying the location of each Pokémon around you. It's different from Xaero's Minimap as it can be configured to only display certain Pokémon, like Shiny or even a specific regional form."]
	quest.5909105DACB265C7.title: "PokéFinder"
	quest.5918E38131653086.quest_desc: [
		"&6Explorer's Compass&r allows you to search for a specific structure. Simply select the structure you're searching for and the compass will point you towards it and how far away it is. Provided it has found the structure."
		""
		"Eyes of Ender are a thing of the past!"
	]
	quest.598680CDD9DB0E52.quest_desc: [
		"&6Chalks&r allow you to draw on a surface. They're great for when you're caving and want to point towards the exit! Sneak right clicking with the chalk will allow you to even choose a symbol to draw, other than arrows."
		""
		"Using &bGlow Ink Sacs&r or &bGlowstone Dust&r on a chalk drawing will make it glow."
		""
		"You can unlock more chalk drawing through certain advancements. Try getting them all!"
	]
	quest.598680CDD9DB0E52.title: "Chalks"
	quest.5A43F7FC6E4542AC.quest_desc: ["&6Fluid Trash Cans&r void any fluid pumped inside of them. They can also be filtered."]
	quest.5AEB947F1B69C2D3.quest_desc: ["&6Water Animal Containers&r work just like &eAnimal Cages&r, just for water animals, like squids."]
	quest.5E81E78CFA243AD3.quest_desc: [
		"Man, I hate having all of my blocks in the inventory so I can use them with the Mech Trowel..."
		""
		"Not anymore! Thanks to the &6AE2 Integration Template&r, you can now link your &eMech Trowel&r to your AE2 system and have the trowel pull from the system!"
	]
	quest.5F905B7F45EED0B5.quest_desc: [
		"The third mode, &9Wand&r, requires it to be unlocked first. You can unlock it with a &6Wand Template&r."
		""
		"Wand mode makes the Mech Trowel act like a &3Building Wand&r, allowing you to place up to 64 blocks at once. It even supports an undo function to fix your 3 last mistakes."
	]
	quest.5F9E9D246EFCAA9F.quest_desc: ["&6Feral Flare Lanterns&r automatically place invisible light sources around itself in dark spots."]
	quest.60E1ED1E150E6CA5.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Personal Shrinking Device&r is a gadget that allows you change size at will!"
		""
		"Right click to open a menu to configure what size you want to change to and then sneak right click the Shrinking Device to change to your desired size. "
		""
		"Although it's called a \"Shrinking\" Device, it also allows you to become bigger as well!"
		""
		"The device requires power to function."
	]
	quest.71AD29F765F5D60C.quest_desc: ["&6Trading Posts&r scan the area around itself for villagers and list all of their trades in its menu."]
	quest.7420E6C97BD0E012.quest_desc: [
		"<wave>Knowledge!</wave>"
		""
		"The &6Eccentric Tome&r is able to consolidate a bunch of guide books into a single item. Simply put it with a guide book in a crafting grid and the tome will absorb the book into itself."
		""
		"Now you can right click to transform the tome into a guide book it has absorbed. If you want to turn the tome back into itself, just left click in the air. This will allow you to transform the tome into another guide book again."
		""
		"If you want to get the guide books back from the tome, simply sneak and press Q to eject all of the guide books inside of the tome. "
	]
	quest.7420E6C97BD0E012.quest_subtitle: "You know what else I like more than materialistic things?"
	quest.7463622B563E9B8B.quest_desc: ["&6Aviaries&r work like the regular &eAnimal Pens&r, except for flying animals."]
	quest.7621511A0AD2A36A.quest_desc: ["Sleep in the same bed three times to unlock this drawing."]
	quest.7621511A0AD2A36A.title: "House"
	quest.7B36099F3D5ED754.quest_desc: ["Tame a pet to unlock this icon."]
	quest.7B36099F3D5ED754.title: "Heart"
	quest.7B8DB91A1C2761EB.quest_desc: [
		"A big hole requires a big tool and the &6Destruction Gadget&r is just the correct tool. Select the size you want to destroy and let the gadget rip."
		""
		"&4All of the blocks it destroys are voided, so don't use this one for mining.&r"
	]
	quest.7D0C401B0AD3ED6F.quest_desc: ["&6FishingNavs&r are &ePokéNavs&r, but for fishing. They show what Pokémon you're currently able to fish up."]
	quest.7EA1E08B1759AC30.quest_desc: ["Dread Lamps stop ambient animals from spawning in a big radius around itself, most notable those <shake>pesky BATS</shake>."]
	task.01A50D1A6237AB17.title: "Any PokéFinder"
	task.1B07999C3EC24EFD.title: "Any Chalk"
	task.3FAFFC2A0DA20F68.title: "Any aviary"
	task.45CADCAAD56F2491.title: "Any PokéNav"
	task.7C1B1FEF1D0B1F38.title: "Any Animal Pen"
}
